WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

01:50.060 --> 01:54.030
<b>Start</b>

01:50.060 --> 01:54.030
<b>Set Timer</b>

01:50.060 --> 01:54.030
<b>AM</b>

01:50.060 --> 01:54.030
<b>AM</b>

02:23.930 --> 02:30.900
<b>Two Opposing Forces</b>

03:17.540 --> 03:18.280
<b>Makki!</b>

03:20.480 --> 03:23.080
<b>Rieko-chan!</b>

03:23.080 --> 03:25.520
<b>Were you... on your way
home from school?</b>

03:25.520 --> 03:26.750
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:28.220 --> 03:30.490
<b>Ah, you got a new cell phone.</b>

03:30.490 --> 03:31.360
<b>Yeah.</b>

03:31.360 --> 03:33.990
<b>That one just came out, right?</b>

03:33.990 --> 03:36.960
<b>There was a game I wanted to play on it...</b>

03:36.960 --> 03:40.360
<b>The game required the new hardware.</b>

03:40.370 --> 03:42.870
<b>The batteries don’t last too long, though.</b>

03:42.870 --> 03:43.830
<b>I see...</b>

03:43.840 --> 03:46.900
<b>Rieko-chan, do you play
cell phone games?</b>

03:46.910 --> 03:48.810
<b>Nope...</b>

03:48.810 --> 03:50.370
<b>I see...</b>

03:52.580 --> 03:53.580
<b>Umm...</b>

03:53.580 --> 03:54.550
<b>What is it?</b>

03:55.410 --> 03:59.150
<b>Have you... ever seen something
you shouldn’t be able to see?</b>

04:00.890 --> 04:04.220
<b>Are you talking about the occult or something...?</b>

04:04.220 --> 04:06.120
<b>Like UFOs or ghosts...?</b>

04:06.760 --> 04:09.430
<b>I’m... not sure.</b>

04:14.000 --> 04:16.870
<b>Well, I don’t think I have.</b>

04:16.870 --> 04:19.240
<b>I don’t have ESP or anything like that.</b>

04:20.110 --> 04:21.640
<b>I see.</b>

04:21.640 --> 04:22.710
<b>Yeah, that makes sense.</b>

04:24.880 --> 04:27.180
<b>Sorry, just forget about it.</b>

04:27.180 --> 04:29.380
<b>See you later, Makki.</b>

04:43.530 --> 04:44.700
<b>I’m home.</b>

04:46.370 --> 04:48.030
<b>Ah, good afternoon.</b>

04:48.030 --> 04:49.500
<b>Oh, welcome back.</b>

04:49.500 --> 04:51.270
<b>Are you helping out Hana-san today?</b>

04:51.270 --> 04:54.010
<b>Yeah. Once I get changed, I’ll be off to Tokimiya.</b>

04:55.370 --> 04:57.780
<b>Helping out Hana-san, you said?</b>

04:57.780 --> 04:59.180
<b>She now has a part-time job.</b>

04:59.180 --> 05:01.350
<b>Ah, that’ll be good.</b>

05:01.350 --> 05:05.550
<b>Working with Hana-san is like
training to be a perfect bride.</b>

05:05.550 --> 05:06.820
<b>I guess so.</b>

05:15.790 --> 05:21.700
<b>Tokimiya</b>

05:20.200 --> 05:21.700
<b>Good afternoon, Hana-san!</b>

05:22.570 --> 05:23.870
<b>You’re early today.</b>

05:24.840 --> 05:26.700
<b>Preparing some hamburger steaks?</b>

05:26.710 --> 05:28.070
<b>Want some help?</b>

05:28.070 --> 05:30.880
<b>Nope. I can’t leave this to you yet.</b>

05:30.880 --> 05:34.450
<b>What? I make them at home, though...</b>

05:34.450 --> 05:39.950
<b>It would affect the taste, which has been
the same at this store for sixty years.</b>

05:39.950 --> 05:44.260
<b>By the time my sixty years of training
is over, I’ll be an old lady.</b>

05:44.260 --> 05:46.290
<b>I didn’t say I wouldn’t teach you how.</b>

05:46.290 --> 05:48.830
<b>You just need to take it one step
at a time before you get there.</b>

05:48.830 --> 05:49.660
<b>That aside...</b>

05:50.700 --> 05:52.430
<b>...what’s wrong?</b>

05:52.430 --> 05:55.270
<b>When you get all formal and
start calling me Hana-<i>san</i>...</b>

05:55.270 --> 05:56.930
<b>...it’s a sign that something’s up.</b>

05:58.070 --> 06:01.170
<b>I can’t hide anything from you, can I?</b>

06:01.170 --> 06:06.150
<b>Kitchen</b>

06:01.170 --> 06:06.150
<b>Tokimiya</b>

06:01.170 --> 06:03.370
<b>Let’s hear it.</b>

06:03.380 --> 06:04.710
<b>Okay.</b>

06:04.710 --> 06:06.140
<b>You see...</b>

